<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-diff-exercises" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Exercises</title>
<p><ol>
				<li>
							<p>
								Decide if the following limits exist and if so evaluate them.
							</p>
				
							<p><ol>
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 3} \frac{2x-1}{3x+2}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 2} \frac{3x-6}{2x}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{2 \sinh{x} -2 \sin{x}}{\cosh{x} - 1}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{e^x + e^{-x} - 2}{1 - \cos{(2x)}}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\sin{(4x)}}{\sin{(6x)}}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{x - \sin{x}}{x^3}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{3x^3 - 6x}{3x+2x^3}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{5x-6}{2x^3}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<me>\lim_{x \to 0} (1+x)^{\frac{1}{x}}</me>
											</p>
								</li>
				
							</ol></p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Using the formal definition of continuity prove that if two functions <m>f</m> and <m>g</m> are both continuous at the point <m>x=a</m> then so is the function <m>f+g</m>.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Prove from first principles that <m>\frac{d}{dx} (x^3) = 3x^2</m>.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Find <m>\frac{dy}{dx}</m> for each of the following functions
							</p>
				
							<p><ol>
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>y=5\cos{(2x)} + 3e^{2x} - 1</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>y= e^{4x} \cos{(2x)}</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>y= \frac{\sin{(2x)}}{x e^x}</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>y= e^{\cos{(3x)}}</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>y=(2x)^{3x} + \sin{(2x^2 - 7e^x)}</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>y=\cos^{-1}{x}</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
							</ol></p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Find the gradients of the following implicitly defined functions <m>y</m> at the points indicated
							</p>
				
							<p><ol>
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>3x^2 + y^2 + 2xy - 6=0</m> at the point <m>(1,1)</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>x^2 + y^2 - 6xy +4x + 4 =0</m> at the point <m>(1,3)</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
							</ol></p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Given that
							</p>
				
							<p><ol>
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>x=5 \cosh{t}</m> and <m>y=4 \sinh{t}</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>x=2 \cos{t}</m> and <m>y=\sin^2{t}</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
								<li>
											<p>
												<m>x=t^2-4</m> and <m>y=t^3 - 4t</m> for <m>-3 \leq t \leq 3</m>
											</p>
								</li>
				
							</ol></p>
				
							<p>
								determine <m>\frac{dy}{dx}</m> and <m>\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}</m> in terms of <m>t</m> for each parametric curve. Sketch these curves using MATLAB.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Find <m>\frac{dy}{dx}</m> where <m>y=(x+3)^{x^2 - 3}</m>.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Find <m>\frac{d}{dx} (\frac{uvw}{z})</m> where <m>u,v,w</m> and <m>z</m> are functions of <m>x</m>.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Suppose that an athletics field consists of a rectangle with semi-circular. Determine the maximum possible area of the rectangular part of the field if the running track around the perimeter of the whole field is to have a length of exactly 400m.
							</p>
				
				<!-- div attr= class="center"-->
							<!-- <figure> -->
					<!-- <image source="gfx/field.PNG"/> -->
								<!-- <caption>image</caption> -->
				<!-- </figure></div attr= class="center"> -->
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Determine the dimensions of a cylindrical food tin of volume 330ml that has minimum surface area.
							</p>
				</li>

				

				<li>
							<p>
								Of all the rectangles having a particular area, which one has the smallest perimeter?
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Of all the rectangles having a particular perimeter, which one has the greatest area?
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								A box with a square base and no top is to have a volume of 3<m>\text{m}^3</m>. Find the dimensions of the box which uses the least amount of material in its construction.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Suppose that a rectangle has two corners lying on the <m>x</m>-axis and the other two lying on the parabola <m>y=8-x^2</m>. Find such a rectangle with maximal area.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								What is the largest rectangle one can inscribe in a circle? That is, find the rectangle of largest area that can fit inside the circle of radius <m>r</m>.
							</p>
				</li>

				<li>
							<p>
								Consider a river that is 0.5 miles wide and runs in a straight line for the purposes of this problem. A pipeline is to be laid across this river and run to a point 3 miles downstream on the opposite bank. Laying pipe under the water is expensive, in fact <m>25\%</m> more expensive per mile than laying pipe on dry land. How should the pipeline be lain across the river in order to minimize the total cost.
							</p>
				</li>

			</ol></p><!--</div attr= class="exer">-->




	
</section>
